WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.350
- There will be days where you're sad,

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.030
there will be days that you're hurting

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:03.863
and there will be days

00:00:03.863 --> 00:00:05.393
that you miss that person more than ever

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.150
but I'm telling you it is so worth it

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.410
and the time that you see them afterwards

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:10.500
is even more worth it

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.043
and it makes it that much more enjoyable.

00:00:13.043 --> 00:00:15.793
(peaceful music)

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.220
I've been in a long relationship

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.670
with my boyfriend named Chris

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.750
who lives about eight hours away from me.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.443
- We're about 3,700 miles apart.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.200
- He's from Norway and I'm from Brazil.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.940
- In August of 2013, I made
the eight-hour plane journey

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.170
to Manchester, England to meet him.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.330
- We met each other at
a website called 7 Cups

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.680
in which we're both volunteer listeners

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.780
to anyone who's going through a rough time

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.970
and even though we started off as friends,

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.453
the more we talked, the more we clicked.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.478
- It was obvious after a
couple months of texting

00:00:48.478 --> 00:00:50.380
that we had a chemistry.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.013
- Being in a long-distance
relationship isn't easy.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.870
- Like sometimes you just
want to pick up your phone

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.762
and order an Uber or just get in your car

00:00:56.762 --> 00:00:58.549
and drive to that person but you can't

00:00:58.549 --> 00:01:00.484
because it's not physically possible.

00:01:00.484 --> 00:01:02.132
- The three most important things for us

00:01:02.132 --> 00:01:05.373
were commitment, trust and communication.

00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:08.510
- Communication is definitely key,

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.813
Skypes, texts, funny
photos, tagging in memes.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.630
- Have scheduled days to like have calls

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.060
or have FaceTime, stuff like that

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.170
to make yourself feel closer to them.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:21.253
- Sometimes we also leave random messages

00:01:21.253 --> 00:01:22.990
on each other's phones.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:25.630
- These things are so much fun

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.510
and they make the distance
so much more bearable.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:31.129
- You have to put in a lot
of trust in each other.

00:01:31.129 --> 00:01:33.260
- It's already hard for
some people to trust

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.690
people that live close to them

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.760
so imagine living miles
and miles away from someone

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.587
and having that trust that
you need to have with them.

00:01:39.587 --> 00:01:41.290
- You know, I was in college

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.380
so I was going to bars and stuff like that

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.810
and there was never a moment
where Joe was jealous at all

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.520
which made it so much easier.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.800
I would just really
work on building trust.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.030
- Once you are able to fully trust them

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.430
and they're able to fully trust you,

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:55.860
it makes it that much easier.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.790
- My biggest tip, being in a
long-distance relationship,

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:01.643
is to always have a trip planned.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.260
- Make a plan with your partner.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.970
- Plan the next time you'll see them

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.640
or plan little trips to see them

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.520
or little trips together
or stuff like that.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.410
Having that motivation,
having that knowledge

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.460
that you know when you'll see them next

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.420
really, really helps with the times

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:15.320
that you're not with them.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.140
- Try to visit as much as possible,

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.826
he visited me this past
March for the whole month

00:02:19.826 --> 00:02:22.973
and I'll be going up there
in July for the whole month.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.100
- Setting up an end goal
and working towards it

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.703
makes a world of a difference.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.490
- This October is exciting
because well be getting married

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:33.000
and hopefully I'll be able
to relocate soon after that.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.383
- We're still together, we are
both in Southern California.

00:02:36.461 --> 00:02:38.770
Hopefully, we're here for the long haul,

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.570
I really wanna be, I love him a lot.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.500
- I'm happy to say that I've
purchased my one-way ticket

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.570
to Manchester to finally
move in with him in December

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.610
and we have set a date

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:56.373
later on in March of 2019 to get married.

00:02:57.147 --> 00:03:01.937
- Long-distance relationships
can be scary and difficult.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.980
- And it's not for
everyone but I feel like

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.240
if you have a strong
connection with that person

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.940
and you really love that person,

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.510
no matter how far they are,

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:12.460
you're gonna always feel their presence

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.010
like they're right next to you

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:17.017
and both of y'all can withstand
anything that comes at you.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.950
- Long-distance relationships
can be difficult

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:23.740
and a lot of people even
say that they're impossible

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:27.190
or they're unrealistic
or they're too difficult

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.983
but I think that if you find someone

00:03:29.983 --> 00:03:32.260
that you don't want to be without,

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:35.070
don't let the distance stop
you from being together.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.823
Distance is temporary.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.860
Good things are worth fighting for.

00:03:38.896 --> 00:03:41.729
(peaceful music)

